Z||000004||88formula||06-27-2001||08:47 PM||||I've seen the 11-13 second four cylinder imports at the track. It's not just something you see in a movie. They are very fast cars. I saw a front wheel drive Honda Civic beat a new C5 corvette in the quarter mile too. Funny thing is the C5 launched real good and the Honda Civic spined the tires for the first 10 feet. I think it was 13.3 vs. 13.5, not sure because that was a year ago.    ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Black88GT||06-27-2001||09:17 PM||||Just because a car runs 10s or 11s in the Quarter doesn't make it the best thing since sliced bread.  The imports that run 10s or 11s are much more rare then the muscle cars that have been doing it for a while.<P>I'll never forget the special on A&E about street racing in Canada, I think it was Toronto.  And they had this guy Mike P or something with a 12 second Civic Hatchback.  I was thinking cool a little cheap pocket rocket, until they interviewed him, he said he has spent over 60 grand (US) on the car.  60 Grand!!  Thats Viper money.  What would you rather drive, a Viper or a Civic HB?<P>All of the imports that run 11s or less share the body of their stock counterparts, and a few other things, but thats about it.  The only reason they do that is to advertise their product.  It's cheaper to spend 100 grand to make Civic run 10s or 11s then it is to buy TV/radio advertisements.  <P>||||reg||1
