Z||000017||TRiAD||06-28-2001||07:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by c m west:<BR><B>Well it is a known fact that a 2.8 Fiero ( manual trans ) WILL destroy either a Honda Prelude or Acura Integra ( same car ). Please do not asked how this theory was proved as it may cause speculation from the "anti-street racing" folks here on Penocks - but no offense to them of course. This "test" has been proved in several Fieros at several intersections and passing lanes - TRUST ME<P><BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR><B>WHOA!</B> Hold the train...<P>1) Honda Prelude is <B>not</B> the same car as an Integra. Now, the Civic Coupe shares most body panels with the 'teg...but you're off to a bad start...<BR>2) Your 2.8 5sp (stock?) is rated at over 8 sec to 60...wrong again...if the 'teg or Prelude driver can drive, you're seeing taillamps. Every time. If it happens to be a Type R or GS-R teg, or an Si Prelude, you wouldn't even be able to read their plates after a blosk or two. <BR>3) "intersections and passing lanes"... Uh, did <I>they</I> know they were racing, genius?<BR>4) "TRUST ME" ...After the "Prelude IS an Integra" dribble you're spouting? See ya. <P>I have nothing against Fieros, I hope to make mine nice and quick, but it's statements like these that <I>really</I> make you lose respect and believability. <P><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
