Z||000023||FieroKyle||06-28-2001||11:15 PM||||One thing, the only people who defend ricers are ricers. Number two, fieros look fast and are fast. Number 3, the blair fiero idea is great! LOL Number 4, I raced a Prelude with the V-Tech, or so it claimed and totallly vintage ricer spoiler with a little asian driving it. It cracked me up so much. I was in my grandpas cargo van and we got at a stoplight together, well, we didn't engage we were racing but I mashed the gas and went, redlined, burned the tires good. Well, next stoplight, I had to turn left. He went straight. He mashed the gas, the tires did the soft squitch and squeel noise with sounded very pathetic. And redlined it all the way, he looked slow, he was slow, the spoiler didn't fool me, lol. He had a big 4 incher tip on the back which made a puking noise. It was so frcken funny. The van I was driving was a 1994 Chevy Astro EXT (cargo version). I have burned out of places in my fiero and almost spun it around before on dry pavement try to see how much of the tires I can smoke, I don't do it hardly much anymore, but its still fun to look back on. I just wished I had my fiero to give that prelude the traditional ricer ass-whooping which I am so sure he is used to.<P>Chill....<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign_1.jpg"> <BR>My Fast 'n Black Car<P>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||1
