Z||000025||JayUSA77||06-29-2001||03:11 AM||||I agree with a lot of you guys out there saying looks aint ****  and most imports are ball-less.  I think were all overlooking the fact that our car are anywhere from 13 to 17 years old and were keeping up with new stock imports. I think thats impressive at any standard and plus look how much it cost to make a import fast.  60K in one case.  A 3000 dollar conversion kit and a 350 and you can have anywhere from 200 to 400 HP all motor in a car that weighs 2500 pounds.  Thats inpressive in my book.  86' Fiero GT<BR>-J||||reg||1
Z||000026||Voytek||06-29-2001||03:02 PM||||Triad - I don't know where you're getting this 'over 8 sec to 60' from.  Go get yourself the Fiero video from the Fiero Store.  Those guys were running an '88 stock formula in the mid 7's from 0 to 60 and it was just slightly behind the supercharged MR2.  No flaming intended, but I've seen this 'over 8 seconds' thing on here before and it's time to set the record straight.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
